`MatchingService` queries a location index rather than iterating every driver — the index is what makes this scale, and the service just consumes it:

```java
Optional<Driver> findNearestDriver(Location pickup) {
    List<Driver> candidates = locationIndex.nearby(pickup, SEARCH_RADIUS_KM);
    return candidates.stream()
        .filter(Driver::isAvailable)
        .min(Comparator.comparingDouble(d -> distance(d.getLocation(), pickup)));
}
```

The filtering happens after the index narrows candidates down from "every driver" to "drivers within a few km" — reversing that order (filter first, then compute distance to all of them) is the mistake the next slides dig into.
